WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.847
This practice example represents one fictional patient record with four different data types.

00:00:07.847 --> 00:00:14.397
Patient_label is text, age is an integer, temperature is a float, and is_follow_up is Boolean.

00:00:14.397 --> 00:00:17.931
The f-strings turn those values into readable output.

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:22.152
Run the example once, then change the values.

00:00:22.152 --> 00:00:26.287
As you edit, ask why each type makes sense.

00:00:26.287 --> 00:00:33.857
You would not average a patient label, but averaging temperatures could be meaningful because temperature is numeric.

00:00:33.857 --> 00:00:38.181
Thinking about meaning and type together is an important data habit.
